# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data lives in GitHub Releases, not in git.
#
# Parquet is compressed binary: git cannot delta it, so every hourly run that
# changed one byte stored a whole new copy forever. Publishing to a release tag
# instead (data-mlb / data-nfl) keeps exactly one copy per filename, and stops
# each data refresh from writing a commit that triggers a Render redeploy.
#
# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#   pitcher_images/     append-only, no churn, and the frontend links it as a
#                       directory -- release assets are a flat namespace.
#   Daily_Props.xlsx    the app reads it but no workflow writes it; it is
#                       maintained by hand, so git is still its home.
#   the legacy *.xlsx   neither written nor read by anything running today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/data/mlb/*.parquet
backend/data/mlb/lineups_*.csv
backend/data/mlb/statcast_*_2026.xlsx
backend/data/mlb/fg_woba_weights.json
backend/data/nfl/*.parquet
backend/data/nfl/on_pace_feed.json
